# Paths of the tools outside the repository. Copy this file as local.env (git ignores it), remove the "#" of what you use
# and put your own paths: NAME=value, without quotes or trailing spaces (spaces inside are fine).
# tools/lsfg/build.sh reads it (android-* targets) and, in the Android port, so do the Makefile (make PLATFORM=android),
# tools/android/apk.sh and tools/android/deps.sh. The same variables in the environment win over this file.
#
# The Android SDK, with build-tools/36.0.0, platforms/android-36, ndk/29.0.14206865 and cmake/4.1.2:
#ANDROID_SDK=C:/Android/Sdk
# The NDK, if it is not in <ANDROID_SDK>/ndk/29.0.14206865:
#NDK=C:/Android/Sdk/ndk/29.0.14206865
# A JDK 17 or newer (javac, java and keytool), for tools/android/apk.sh:
#JDK=C:/Program Files/Eclipse Adoptium/jdk-21
# The Python that tools/android/apk.sh puts the APK together with (by default build/gen-venv/Scripts/python.exe, made by
# `make build/gen-venv/.ok`):
#PY=C:/path/to/python.exe
# A ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz already downloaded, for tools/android/deps.sh (without it, it is downloaded from ffmpeg.org):
#FFMPEG_TAR=C:/path/to/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz
